findings.body:
The goal was to drop a redundant `.clone()`. The edit also swapped the message variant:

::diff{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="1712-1722"}

Now `WryWebviewDispatcher::delete_cookie` puts `WebviewMessage::SetCookie(cookie)` on the event loop. The handler at line 3731 calls `webview.set_cookie(&cookie)`, so any call to `Webview::delete_cookie` / `WebviewWindow::delete_cookie` writes the cookie again (or creates it) instead of removing it. Nothing constructs `WebviewMessage::DeleteCookie` anymore, which means the handler at line 3737 can never run.

::callout{type="warning"}
The failure is silent. The call returns `Ok(())`, so a logout flow that deletes a session cookie would leave the session in place.

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="1718-1718"}
        WebviewMessage::DeleteCookie(cookie.into_owned()),

There is no test covering `set_cookie` versus `delete_cookie` dispatch, which is why this got through.

The reordered lines have irregular spacing that rustfmt would rewrite:

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1315-1322"}

`size.width,    size.height` has extra spaces and `position.x,position.y` is missing one. AGENTS.md rule 3 requires `cargo fmt --all -- --check` to pass, so CI will reject this. Also, the order of the two `if let` blocks makes no difference: both only store values on the window builder. The reorder isn't needed and only adds diff noise.

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1316-1322"}
    if let Some(size) = features.size() {
      self.window_builder = self.window_builder.inner_size(size.width, size.height);
    }

    if let Some(position) = features.position() {
      self.window_builder = self.window_builder.position(position.x, position.y);
    }

::diff{file="examples/api/src-tauri/src/lib.rs" lines="76-77"}

`created_window_count` is moved into the closure and only used through `fetch_add(&self, ..)`, so the `mut` binding is never needed. rustc emits `unused_mut`, and with `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` (AGENTS.md rule 2) that warning becomes an error. This was already present in the base, but since the PR moves these lines anyway, it's a good time to drop the `mut`.

::suggestion{file="examples/api/src-tauri/src/lib.rs" lines="77-77"}
        let created_window_count = std::sync::atomic::AtomicUsize::new(0);
